          "text": "Critique becomes actionable when comments are anchored to visible evidence. Instead of saying, 'This plan is confusing,' point to the crossing circulation paths and say, 'Visitors arriving here meet two equally prominent routes, so orientation is uncertain. Which destination should be visually primary? ' The annotation records an observation, its consequence, and a design question. It does not prescribe the only answer or evaluate the designer as a person. This structure preserves authorship while making the review precise enough to revisit during revision."
