          "text": "No single drawing tells the full story. The site plan explains approach and context. The floor plan reveals circulation and adjacencies. The section shows level changes, daylight, structure, and vertical relationships. Elevations describe public face and environmental response, while details test whether the envelope can actually perform. A strong review traces one design question across all of them. For example: can a visitor move from sidewalk to entrance, reception, and classroom without ambiguity or barriers? Contradictions between drawings become high-value revision targets."
